abstract: >-
  Community-maintained lecture materials on machine learning
  interpretability for SCC5819 Topics in Artificial Intelligence, a
  graduate course at ICMC-USP taught by Prof. Andre Carlos Ponce de Leon
  Ferreira de Carvalho, following Christoph Molnar's Interpretable
  Machine Learning from chapter 12 onward, one lecture module per
  chapter. Each module is a fully reproducible, real-data walkthrough on
  the Breast Cancer Wisconsin (Diagnostic) dataset, pairing a lecture
  notebook with a technical companion that measures the method's
  behaviour rather than restating its documentation. Modules share one
  model, one split and one patient, so they read as a single case. The
  seed module is LIME (chapter 14), including a line-by-line validation
  of the lime package internals; the remaining chapters are open for
  contribution.
